      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): bound finished bash process session retention",
        "body": "Closes #105625\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where long-running Gateways retaining many completed background bash/exec sessions would keep an unbounded finished-session map until TTL expiry, and session reset/delete would leave matching finished process records pollable until that TTL. That multiplies retained aggregate output and can grow gateway heap under bursty shell workloads.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nKeep completed `process poll` / `process log` aggregates (ClawSweeper rejected tail-only retention), but enforce deterministic finished-session count and total-aggregate-byte caps, and purge finished records whose `scopeKey` matches gateway session lifecycle cleanup keys. Shared scopes (for example chat bash) are not purged when an unrelated agent session resets.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators get bounded finished-process memory growth under heavy background exec traffic. Resetting or deleting a gateway session no longer leaves that session’s finished process records pollable until job TTL. Completed process log/poll behavior for still-retained sessions is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nVerification host: local macOS Darwin arm64 (live runtime harness on PR head + focused unit tests)\n\nLive runtime (agent-solo, not Vitest) — see **Real behavior proof** for full redacted transcript:\n- Production count cap 50: 51 completed background sessions → 50 retained; oldest unpollable; newest pollable with aggregate\n- Production aggregate cap 2,000,000: two 1.2M sessions → only newest retained (1.2M total)\n- Scoped reset: `clearSessionResetRuntimeState([\"agent:main:main\"])` → `finishedProcessSessionsCleared=1`; `chat:bash` retained\n\nFocused tests (pass, supplemental):\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-process-registry.test.ts` — 18 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/session-reset-cleanup.test.ts` — 7 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-tools.process.poll-timeout.test.ts` — 8 passed\n\nStatic:\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check` on touched files — pass\n- `git diff --check` — pass\n\nCompatibility note for maintainers: this PR **accepts bounded early eviction** (CS recommended option). Completed process poll/log may disappear before TTL when budgets are exceeded; refine thresholds only if a longer delayed-poll contract is required.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior addressed: Finished bash process sessions are hard-capped (50 sessions / 2,000,000 aggregate characters) so completed `process poll`/`process log` retention cannot grow unbounded until TTL; session reset/delete purges finished records only for matching lifecycle `scopeKey` values (shared scopes such as `chat:bash` stay).\n- Compatibility stance (CS recommended option: **Prove and accept bounded eviction**): Contributor accepts the proposed internal limits. Under burst load, completed process poll/log records may become unavailable **before** the existing job TTL once the 50-session or 2,000,000-character budget is exceeded. Thresholds are intentionally product-owned if maintainers later want a longer delayed-poll window.\n- Environment: local macOS Darwin arm64, Node v24.17.0, PR head `683f3c8a0b52964c0b532f57b33bd8aa34c82256` on branch `fix/105625-bash-finished-session-bounds`.\n- Current-main contrast: On main, `pruneFinishedSessions` only deletes by TTL; `finishedSessions` has no count/byte cap; `clearSessionResetRuntimeState` does not touch finished process records, so scoped finished sessions remain pollable until TTL.\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch (live runtime harness, **not** Vitest):\n  1. Load production owner modules from this checkout: `src/agents/bash-process-registry.ts` and `src/auto-reply/reply/session-reset-cleanup.ts` via `tsx`.\n  2. Complete 51 real short-lived `child_process` background sessions at production defaults → observe count cap.\n  3. Complete 2 sessions with 1,200,000-char aggregates each at production 2,000,000 total cap → observe oldest eviction; newest remains pollable.\n  4. Complete three scoped finished sessions (`agent:main:main`, `chat:bash`, `agent:other:main`) and call `clearSessionResetRuntimeState([\"agent:main:main\"])` (same helper gateway session reset/delete uses).\n- Evidence after fix (redacted live transcript, 2026-07-13T05:21:16Z UTC):\n\n```text\n=== Live runtime proof: finished bash session retention bounds ===\nhost: darwin arm64\nnode: v24.17.0\nbranch_head: 683f3c8a0b52964c0b532f57b33bd8aa34c82256\nmethod: real child_process echo sessions; production finished caps 50 / 2_000_000; not Vitest\nredaction: no tokens/paths/IPs; synthetic ids only\n\n--- A) count cap at production default (50 sessions) ---\ncompleted_background_execs: 51\nfinished_retained_count: 50\ncount-00_pollable: false\ncount-50_pollable: true\ncount-50_aggregate: \"out-50\\n\"\ncount_cap_ok: true\n\n--- B) aggregate-char cap at production default (2_000_000) ---\nsessions_completed: 2 x 1200000 chars\nfinished_retained_count: 1\nretained_ids: bytes-new\ntotal_aggregated_chars: 1200000\nbytes-old_pollable: false\nbytes-new_pollable: true\naggregate_cap_ok: true\n\n--- C) clearSessionResetRuntimeState scoped finished-process purge ---\nbefore_reset finished_count=3\nbefore match=true shared=true other=true\nreset_keys: [\"agent:main:main\"]\nfinishedProcessSessionsCleared: 1\nafter_reset finished_count=2\nafter match=false shared=true other=true\nscoped_reset_ok: true\n\n=== summary ===\ncount_cap_ok=true\naggregate_cap_ok=true\nscoped_reset_ok=true\noverall_ok=true\n```\n\n- Control check: Scope purge only matches exact `scopeKey` values; `chat:bash` and `agent:other:main` remain after resetting `agent:main:main`. Retained finished sessions keep full `aggregated` (not tail-only) for poll/log.\n- Observed result after fix: Oldest finished sessions are evicted under production count and total-aggregate caps while retained entries stay pollable; session-reset runtime cleanup removes only matching-scope finished process records and reports `finishedProcessSessionsCleared`.\n- Supplemental focused unit tests (still pass; not a substitute for the live harness above):\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/bash-process-registry.test.ts` — 18 passed\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/session-reset-cleanup.test.ts` — 7 passed\n- What was not tested: Full multi-tenant Control UI reset UX; sustained multi-hour production heap profile under mixed channel traffic (live harness exercises the same in-process registry and reset cleanup path the Gateway process uses).\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nThis fix was authored with AI assistance (Grok). Implementation and proof follow ClawSweeper guidance on #105625 (count-plus-byte retention + scope-keyed cleanup; keep completed aggregates).\n\n",
